social media accounts claiming to represent the Iranian military show signs of being part of so-called content farms. DW Fact Check looks at how they operate and how users can spot them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy slaps Meta with €805mn fine over access to Android photos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f4c591e30416892206ba9bd674efa3634c629e82a3cdc78eaac0fa656c9eb33</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:50Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T18:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-slaps-meta-with-_805mn-fine-over-access-to-android-photos/a-79949032--51e9f2bddd4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-slaps-meta-with-€805mn-fine-over-access-to-android-photos/a-79949032?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Italian regulators say Meta accessed photos and multimedia content from Italian users via the Facebook application for Android devices. Meta has not yet commented on the fine or the allegations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Protesters, UN urge swift climate deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65480349450b49608c30baf2bcc693270987d0b15c0e0318782cc24247c10d97</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:49:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-protesters-un-urge-swift-climate-deal/a-79948501--5f86c2781d9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-protesters-un-urge-swift-climate-deal/a-79948501?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UN climate chief has warned that "tactical delays" at the COP31 climate talks in Turkey could prevent a deal to slow global warming.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Holzer Prize awarded to Katja Gloger and DW's Jaafar Abdul Karim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97d06bd87c4e30e66faeceaf2558d83ec0217aa3eef5e67364360e9f59a0c252</id><updated>2026-11-14T20:4